{"availability":"available","full":"cortexapps/engrams","name":"engrams","description":"AI software factory for the enterprise","category":"Other","language":"Rust","stars":39,"forks":2,"created":"2026-04-27T23:32:01Z","updated":"2026-10-01T18:38:34Z","license":"AGPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://engramsfactory.com/","topics":["agent","agentic-development-environment","ai-agent","ai-agents","sandbox-environment","sandbox-environments","software-factory"],"demo":null,"color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T08:24:09.857Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-03T08:24:09.857Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-03T08:24:09.857Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T08:24:09.857Z","discoveredVia":[],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T08:24:09.857Z","stars":39,"forks":2}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["engrams is a self-hosted orchestrator for AI coding agents. It runs each agent in its own Firecracker microVM, snapshots the VM when the agent goes idle, and restores it when the next prompt arrives.","A session is a plain OCI image plus an agent harness. You build the image with docker build, enable it once, and engrams boots it on a host in your own cloud, streams the transcript and tool calls to the dashboard, Slack, or the CLI, and snapshots the VM away when it goes quiet. Claude Code and Codex ship as harnesses. The pattern is the one behind hosted sandbox products like E2B, Modal Sandboxes, and Ramp's Inspect; engrams is the version you run yourself."],"features":["It runs in your cloud. One Terraform apply and two Helm releases bring it up on GKE or EKS, with GCS or S3 for blobs and your cloud's secret manager for credentials. No transcript, workspace, or key leaves your account.","Every session is a real virtual machine. Isolation is KVM, enforced by hardware, not a container boundary. Outbound traffic from a session goes through a filtering proxy on the host, so an agent reaches only the hosts…","Idle sessions cost nothing to keep. When an agent stops talking, engrams snapshots the VM's memory and disk into content-addressed chunks and destroys the VM. The next prompt restores it: under 100 ms on the same host,…","Storage is deduplicated by construction. Chunks are keyed by their hash, so a base image is stored once no matter how many sessions use it. A thousand sessions of a 4 GiB image take about 100 GiB, not 4 TiB.","Your image stays yours. The agent runtime, the in-guest daemon, and the tools are staged by the host and mounted into the VM at boot. The image contract is any Linux image with /bin/sh."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/cortexapps/engrams/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"9e764ae09048f69d493a885a4a541ac658eb52e593dfe2049d3b16a1d9dba275","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T08:24:09.857Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T14:17:51.565Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"engrams is a self-hosted orchestrator for AI coding agents. It runs each agent in its own Firecracker microVM, snapshots the VM when the agent goes idle, and restores it when the next prompt arrives.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/cortexapps/engrams/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Tilt's status page is at and the dashboard is at Open the dashboard and create an account; registration is open in the dev stack.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/cortexapps/engrams/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"9e764ae09048f69d493a885a4a541ac658eb52e593dfe2049d3b16a1d9dba275","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/cortexapps/engrams/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-03T14:17:51.566Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-01T18:38:34Z","overviewAttemptAt":"2026-10-03T14:17:45.380Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/cortexapps/engrams/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-03T14:17:51.567Z","hash":"9e764ae09048f69d493a885a4a541ac658eb52e593dfe2049d3b16a1d9dba275","originalBytes":10751,"storedBy